{
  "name": "diving-beetle",
  "_about": "The great diving beetle (Dytiscus marginalis), 3.2 cm long: a smooth streamlined oval, flattish, very glossy dark olive-black with a yellow rim round the pronotum and the wing cases and a yellow band across the face; thread antennae; the hind legs long flattened OARS fringed with golden swimming hairs, the front and middle legs small and brown. A fierce hunter of ponds. Written whole by tools/creaturegen/rework/insects/beetles.py on insectlib.py (six jointed legs on a tripod gait, the antennae on bones of their own that wave).",
